> 
> 
> cleanEx()
> nameEx("reportNPAV")
> ### * reportNPAV
> 
> flush(stderr()); flush(stdout())
> 
> ### Name: reportNPAV
> ### Title: Generate the Latex-text based on the NPAV by Lüpsen (see
> ###   <https://www.uni-koeln.de/~luepsen/R/>). Only significant main and
> ###   interaction effects are reported. P-values are rounded for the third
> ###   digit and partial eta squared values are provided when possible.
> ###   Attention: the independent variables of the formula and the term
> ###   specifying the participant must be factors (i.e., use as.factor()).
> ### Aliases: reportNPAV
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> model <- data.frame(
+   Df = c(1, 1, 10),
+   `F value` = c(6.12, 5.01, NA),
+   `Pr(>F)` = c(0.033, 0.045, NA),
+   check.names = FALSE
+ )
> rownames(model) <- c("Video", "gesture:eHMI", "Residuals")
> reportNPAV(model, dv = "mental workload")
Warning in reportNPAV(model, dv = "mental workload") :
  reportNPAV() is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use reportART() with ARTool instead.
The NPAV found a significant main effect of \Video on mental workload (\F{1}{10}{6.12}, \p{0.033}), $\eta_{p}^{2}$=0.38 [0.02, 1.00]. 
The NPAV found a significant interaction effect of \gesture $\times$ \eHMI on mental workload (\F{1}{10}{5.01}, \p{0.045}), $\eta_{p}^{2}$=0.33 [0.00, 1.00]. 
> 
> 
> 
